{"annotations":[{"kind":"ceiling_change","label":"issuance ceiling cut","x":"2025-10-29"}],"as_of":"2026-11-11T23:02:37+00:00","bands":[],"caveat":"The gray line compounds the nominal ceiling as it mints, so a full year at today's 2.50% allows 2.53%; growth of 2.48% sits below both.","caveat_template":"The gray line compounds the nominal ceiling as it mints, so a full year at today's {i_max_now} allows {ceiling_365}; growth of {g_365} sits below both.","claims":["H1"],"code_ref":"pipeline/models/supply.py::rolling_growth","coverage":{"first":"2020-10-15","gaps":[],"last":"2026-11-10","n":639},"empty_state":null,"eyebrow":"O1 · tests H1","form":"line","formula_ids":["F-growth","F-ceiling","F-mint-check"],"id":"c02","notes":["Samples are monthly until 2022-04-04, weekly until 2025-10-06 and daily since, so the line grows denser to the right.","The gray line switches rate at the exact block of each ceiling change.","Over the last year the 1,201 epochs minted at the ceiling with a median gap of -0.008 pp, from -0.410 pp to -0.001 pp."],"notes_templates":["Samples are monthly until {rpc_weekly_from}, weekly until {rpc_daily_from} and daily since, so the line grows denser to the right.","The gray line switches rate at the exact block of each ceiling change.","Over the last year the {n_mint_epochs_365} epochs minted at the ceiling with a median gap of {mint_vs_ceiling_median_365_pp}, from {mint_vs_ceiling_min_365_pp} to {mint_vs_ceiling_max_365_pp}."],"panels":[],"priority":"lead","queries":[{"body_or_sql":"{\n  \"id\": \"near_rpc\",\n  \"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\",\n  \"method\": \"block\",\n  \"params\": {\n    \"block_id\": 224129519\n  }\n}","endpoint":"https://archival-rpc.mainnet.fastnear.com","file":"data/raw/rpc/history_samples.csv","kind":"jsonrpc"},{"body_or_sql":"{\n  \"id\": \"near_rpc\",\n  \"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\",\n  \"method\": \"EXPERIMENTAL_protocol_config\",\n  \"params\": {\n    \"block_id\": 224129519\n  }\n}","endpoint":"https://archival-rpc.mainnet.fastnear.com","file":"data/raw/rpc/history_samples.csv","kind":"jsonrpc"},{"body_or_sql":"{\n  \"id\": \"near_rpc\",\n  \"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\",\n  \"method\": \"block\",\n  \"params\": {\n    \"block_id\": \"<epoch boundary height>\"\n  }\n}","endpoint":"https://archival-rpc.mainnet.fastnear.com","file":"data/raw/rpc/epoch_history.csv","kind":"jsonrpc"},{"body_or_sql":"-- name: daily_supply_flows\n-- description: End-of-day total supply and the gross mint and burn behind it, from the per-block change in blocks.total_supply (yoctoNEAR, FLOAT64) ordered by block_height. Supply only rises at epoch boundaries (validator and treasury reward mint) and only falls through burns, so positive deltas are summed as minted_near and negative deltas as burnt_near; the boundary block's own burn is netted into its mint. epoch_boundaries counts deltas above 10 NEAR. The query also reads @start_date - 1 so the first block of the range has a predecessor, then drops that day. A day whose first block has no predecessor in the previous calendar day (a gap in the table) gets empty mint, burn and boundary counts instead of a delta that spans the gap; genesis day 2020-07-21 is exempt. burnt_near is total supply destruction (fee burn net of the 30% contract reward, plus any other burn), not gross fees.\n-- grain: one row per block_date\n-- params: @start_date DATE, @end_date DATE (inclusive block_date range; the query reads block_date from @start_date - 1 for the LAG and drops that day)\n-- est: 0.002 GB/day (blocks: block_date, block_height, total_supply = 24 bytes x ~78k blocks/day, DERIVED from the Nov 2024 table size; recent days are heavier, the dry run is authoritative)\nWITH block_supply AS (\n  SELECT\n    block_date,\n    block_height,\n    CAST(total_supply AS FLOAT64) AS total_supply\n  FROM `bigquery-public-data.crypto_near_mainnet_us.blocks`\n  WHERE block_date BETWEEN DATE_SUB(@start_date, INTERVAL 1 DAY) AND @end_date\n),\ndeltas AS (\n  SELECT\n    block_date,\n    block_height,\n    total_supply,\n    total_supply - LAG(total_supply) OVER chain AS supply_delta,\n    LAG(block_date) OVER chain AS prev_block_date\n  FROM block_supply\n  WINDOW chain AS (ORDER BY block_height)\n),\ndays AS (\n  SELECT\n    block_date,\n    ARRAY_AGG(total_supply IGNORE NULLS ORDER BY block_height DESC LIMIT 1)[SAFE_OFFSET(0)] AS eod_supply,\n    SUM(IF(supply_delta > 0, supply_delta, 0)) AS minted,\n    SUM(IF(supply_delta < 0, -supply_delta, 0)) AS burnt,\n    COUNTIF(supply_delta > 1e25) AS boundaries,\n    LOGICAL_AND(\n      block_date = DATE '2020-07-21'\n      OR (supply_delta IS NOT NULL AND DATE_DIFF(block_date, prev_block_date, DAY) <= 1)\n    ) AS deltas_complete\n  FROM deltas\n  WHERE block_date BETWEEN @start_date AND @end_date\n  GROUP BY block_date\n)\nSELECT\n  block_date,\n  eod_supply / 1e24 AS eod_supply_near,\n  IF(deltas_complete, minted / 1e24, NULL) AS minted_near,\n  IF(deltas_complete, burnt / 1e24, NULL) AS burnt_near,\n  IF(deltas_complete, boundaries, NULL) AS epoch_boundaries\nFROM days\nORDER BY block_date\n","endpoint":"bigquery-public-data.crypto_near_mainnet_us","file":"sql/daily_supply_flows.sql","kind":"sql"}],"reference_lines":[{"label":"zero","y":0}],"section":"O1","sentence":"Blue is how much NEAR's supply grew over the trailing year at each sample date; gray is the most the issuance ceiling allowed over the same window, and a point below zero would mean supply shrank.","sentence_template":"Blue is how much NEAR's supply grew over the trailing year at each sample date; gray is the most the issuance ceiling allowed over the same window, and a point below zero would mean supply shrank.","series":[{"dashed":false,"entity":"near","id":"g_365","label":"NEAR supply growth, trailing year","panel":null,"points":[["2021-11-01",4.9888],["2021-12-01",4.9461],["2022-01-01",4.9692],["2022-02-01",5.0039],["2022-03-01",5.0384],["2022-04-01",5.0634],["2022-04-04",5.0568],["2022-04-25",5.0634],["2022-05-01",5.0691],["2022-05-02",5.0639],["2022-05-30"